    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras feature a high-ceiling lineup today, led by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.58) and **Junior Caminero** (80.71). **Yordan Alvarez** is the premier start, benefiting from an elite 0.476 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Trey Yesavage. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** secures the highest park factor boost (+14%) on the slate, making him an essential anchor in the UTIL spot. **Trea Turner** (77.43) and **Kyle Schwarber** (75.47) also stand out as elite options against Carson Palmquist, where their combination of leadoff/top-order positioning and dynamic platoon advantages provide a significant buffer against the expected pitching floor. **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) warrants attention as well, leveraging a massive +19% SP skill advantage against Randy V\u00e1squez to earn his spot in the outfield.\n\nPlatoon advantages are driving the bulk of our secondary production, most notably for **Christian Yelich** (56.33) and **Josh Smith** (57.92), who both capitalize on dynamic platoon splits to maintain relevance despite difficult matchups or lower lineup positioning. The most difficult bench decision involved **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (47.32), who narrowly missed the cut. While his speed profile is high, he was forced out by the combination of an elite pitching matchup against Tarik Skubal and negative platoon adjustments, dropping his efficiency below the threshold. We are monitoring all lineups closely, as the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board\u2014particularly for **Gary Sanchez**, **Colt Keith**, and **Caleb Durbin**\u2014introduces volatility; should **Colt Keith** or **Gary Sanchez** slide further down in the order, their marginal scores could dip into the below-floor category, though we currently value **Colt Keith** for the stolen base potential provided by the slow delivery of Emerson Hancock.",
